# Local Hindsight

Dashboard: http://localhost:9999. API: http://localhost:8888.

## CLI client

The official `hindsight` CLI 0.9.2 is installed at `~/.local/bin/hindsight`,
already on PATH. Its user configuration at `~/.hindsight/config` points to
`http://127.0.0.1:8888`. No client API key is configured for this loopback-only
deployment; the server's 9router credentials remain separate.

```sh
hindsight --version
hindsight bank list --output json
hindsight --help
```

`HINDSIGHT_API_URL` and `HINDSIGHT_API_KEY` override saved settings. Named
profiles can also select another deployment; neither override is configured here.
The global `hindsight-docs` skill at `~/.agents/skills/hindsight-docs/` is discovered
by Codex. Automatic ingestion is provided separately by the coding-agent integration.

## Codex shared memory

The official `@vectorize-io/hindsight-coding-agents` runtime is installed under
`~/.hindsight/coding-agents/`, initially version 0.5.3, through its supported npx
update path. It connects only to `http://127.0.0.1:8888` and uses the single
`shared` bank across projects. Project tags/metadata retain provenance without
creating separate banks. Settings live in `~/.hindsight/coding-agent.json`.

- Global `~/.codex/hooks.json` registers SessionStart, UserPromptSubmit and Stop.
  Automatic context and transcript write-back begin in a new Codex session.
- `~/.codex/config.toml` enables hooks and registers the integration's stdio MCP
  adapter as `hindsight`; it replaces the initial generic HTTP registration.
- `~/.codex/AGENTS.md` describes the authorized shared-memory workflow. Both
  `hindsight-docs` and `hindsight-coding-agent` are global Codex skills under
  `~/.agents/skills/`. Codex's internal memory implementation is not replaced.
- `retainSessions=true`, `autoSeed=true`, `gitIngest="full"`: live conversations
  and progressive recent Git history are captured automatically. Upstream 0.5.3
  limits automatic Git deepening to the newest 300 commits, 50 diffs per run;
  this is not an unlimited import of all historical commits or conversations.
- `autoUpdate=true`: session starts check at most daily and update only the
  Hindsight coding-agent runtime through npx. Container images remain pinned.
- `codebaseSurvey=true`: memory-only headless surveys use the configured Codex
  model with a read-only sandbox. Survey children keep MCP access but disable
  automatic hooks to prevent recursion. This does not authorize adding model
  launchers back to the BOF3 harness or disabling approval controls.
- `maxParallelRetains=2`, shared observation scope, low reflect budget. Automatic
  capture can contain sensitive conversation text; do not paste secrets into it.

MCP initialization and bank routing were verified from two different workspaces.
A synthetic Stop-hook transcript was retained, recalled and then deleted.
Receipts and private pre-change backups are in `~/.local/state/hindsight/`.
Restart Codex to load the new MCP connection, hooks and global instructions.

## One-time Pi/docs migration

The requested import uses `~/.local/share/hindsight/imports/pi-docs-20260910/`.
Its `manifest.sqlite3` holds source hashes, normalized documents and stable batch
operation IDs; `receipt.json` distinguishes accepted uploads from completed server
processing. The original Pi files and project documents are not modified.

Sources are both `.pi/memory/memory.db` stores, this project's `docs/`, this
project's `.pi/sessions/`, and `~/.pi/agent/sessions/`, including nested history.
SQLite snapshots preserve audit events and tombstoned lessons without reactivating
deleted memories. Conversation conversion keeps user/assistant text and saved
compaction/branch summaries, with timestamps and parent-entry provenance; reasoning,
tool-output dumps, binary attachments and injected custom context are omitted.
Recognizable credentials are redacted, but pattern matching is not a guarantee that
every sensitive natural-language detail is removed.

```sh
python3 ~/.local/share/hindsight/imports/pi-docs-20260910/migration.py report
python3 ~/.local/share/hindsight/imports/pi-docs-20260910/migration.py status
python3 ~/.local/share/hindsight/imports/pi-docs-20260910/migration.py upload
```

`upload` resumes only unacknowledged batches; fixed operation IDs prevent duplicate
queueing after a lost acknowledgement. It queues work for Hindsight's asynchronous
worker rather than claiming extraction has finished. This migration does not scan
unrelated home files or bulk-import old Codex conversations.

