Environment edits require container recreation, not merely `docker restart`.
The user units run `docker compose up` to reconcile configuration changes. Do not
run a separate detached Compose controller alongside them. Never delete the data
directory while recreating containers. Initialization SQL runs only on an empty
database; credential rotation later requires SQL changes as well as file updates.
Do not print, share or commit environment/initialization files. Upgrades are manual.

## Models and database

- LLM: `qwen-combo` through local 9router's OpenAI-compatible API.
- Embeddings: `qwen3-chat/qwen3-embeddings`, preserving all 4096 dimensions.
- Reranker: local FlashRank `ms-marco-MiniLM-L-12-v2`.
- Database: VectorChord 1.1.1 / PostgreSQL 18, configured as `vchord`.
- Hindsight: official 0.9.2 image; both container digests are pinned in Compose.

The sole enabled existing 9router key is reused for the two model clients. No
Codex OAuth credentials are copied or mounted. The skill supplies documentation;
it does not automatically ingest project files. The unsuccessful embedded-DB
index-threshold workaround is removed, not bypassed.

## Isolation

Both Hindsight containers use `network_mode: host` by explicit user request.
API `127.0.0.1:8888`, dashboard `127.0.0.1:9999` and PostgreSQL
`127.0.0.1:5432` listen only on loopback. Model clients reach the host 9router
at `http://127.0.0.1:20128/v1`; the database URL also uses `127.0.0.1`.
Host networking removes network-namespace/egress isolation: containers can
reach host listeners and host-routed networks. Do not describe this as an
internal isolated Docker network. Private backups under
`~/.local/state/hindsight/host-network-*/` retain the former configuration.

Both containers run as the unprivileged host UID/GID with all capabilities
dropped, no-new-privileges, read-only root filesystems, scoped writable bind
mounts/tmpfs, and CPU/memory/PID limits. Each container has a 4 GiB `/dev/shm`
ceiling and a two-CPU quota. Shared memory is allocated on demand, not reserved;
it also counts toward the unchanged total-memory limits (app 3 GiB, database
2 GiB), so the full shared-memory ceiling is not usable within those limits.
Hindsight's database role is not a
superuser; bootstrap administration has a separate credential. Docker remains a
privileged host service: users with Docker access can inspect container secrets.

The optional upstream unauthenticated dependency wait is disabled; ordinary
authenticated provider validation remains enabled. Do not misdeclare embedding
dimensions or switch to incompatible pgvector HNSW settings.

The attached Compose controllers return 130 when interrupted during an orderly
systemd stop, even when their containers exit 0. Both units recognize that
controller status as successful; unexpected exits still restart the controllers.

## Recursive repository import: explicitly authorized

The prepared corpus is private and local at
`~/.local/share/hindsight/imports/repositories-20260910/`:
26,750 unique files across 77 repository roots, packed into 10,346 records.
Another 274 files were covered by earlier accepted imports and 3,118 exact
duplicates were excluded. Sources were not modified.

Approval review initially blocked upload because the configured 9router/Qwen route
could forward code or documentation to an external provider. After that risk was
explained, the user explicitly authorized uploading this full corpus. The original
resumable uploader was then approved, without changing any safety settings or using
an alternate transport. `authorization.json` records this scope; `receipt.json`
records acknowledged batches and `processing.json` records the last extraction
status check. Earlier acknowledged imports are separate.

The local inventory, exclusion policy, converted data, source hashes, provenance
and redaction counts remain in `inventory.sqlite3`, `policy.py`,
`manifest.sqlite3` and `receipt.json`. `migration.py report` reads the local
receipt data. Preparation and queue acceptance must not be described as completed
extraction; existing Qwen inference probes also exposed intermittent failures.

